  "graded_by": [
    {
      "unit": "U2",
      "test": "core/internal/worker/rediscover_test.go — the v0.2 order: spool, dial, version branch for live peers only; a retained ended session replayed before its spooled end; an audited session's spool entry ignored"
    },
    {
      "unit": "U11",
      "test": "harness/rigs/kill-core.sh — SIGKILL the core while a session ends on the target; on restart the spooled end is replayed and written, once"
    }
  ],
  "description": "What a v0.2 core restarted after kill -9 does, in its order (worker-manifest.schema.json; the v0.1 rule c5-rediscovery keeps its meaning). 1. The spool first: fixture-session-f ended while the core was away and its worker has since exited, so its end is the spooled one — never E10 worker_lost; fixture-session-g's entry is for a session the core already audited, and is ignored, because a session ends once. 2. The dial, as v0.1: fixture-conn-2's control socket refuses, so fixture-session-c is terminated / worker_lost, whatever the manifest's version — but fixture-session-h, whose socket refuses inside a live connection, ended while the core was away and its end is in the spool: it is written from the spool, never read as worker_lost. 3. The version branch, for live peers only: fixture-worker-3 has no proto_version, so fixture-session-d is unreachable / protocol; fixture-worker-1 speaks 0.2, so its sessions get the handshake — fixture-session-e among them, an ended session the worker still retains, which is replayed before the core writes its spooled end. The supervisor carries 0.2, so workers may be created through it.",
  "corpus": [
    "immortality §2.1",
    "immortality §3",
    "immortality §6.4",
    "session model §9 E10",
    "session model §15",
    "decision 5.38",
    "decision 5.44"
  ],
